{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"celestine-treasonous-ewe","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe plan-review harness needs a frozen, versioned corpus of past reviews it can replay. `plan_review_result_v2` sidecars (written by `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py`) already retain the Pass-1 findings, Pass-2 answer vectors and Pass-3 outputs per finding, but (a) `sidecar.prune` has deleted ~5,000 `REVIEW_RESULT` files from the tree (recoverable from `origin/tickets` history; `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/harnesses/mine_outcome_corpus.py` already walks git objects this way), (b) the reviewed plan text is stored only as `material_fingerprint`, and (c) compaction has folded most pre-review `EDIT` events into `SNAPSHOT`s, so the at-review description must be reconstructed from git history. The `~/legacy-modernization-navigator` store (74 sidecars, different project overlay) should be included for overlay diversity.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py`:\n\n1. Enumerate sidecars from a list of store roots (each a tickets-branch checkout or a git ref), reading tree files plus deleted `*-REVIEW_RESULT.json` blobs from history (`git log --diff-filter=D --name-only` then `git show <commit>^:<path>`). Keep only `data.schema in {plan_review_result_v1, plan_review_result_v2}`; record schema version, `impact_model_version`, `regver`, `verified_at_sha`, `provider_provenance.ran_model`, `review_phase`.\n2. Reconstruct the reviewed material per sidecar: replay `CREATE`/`EDIT` (tree + history-deleted) up to the sidecar timestamp for description and file_impact, resolve child pins from `reviewed_related_material`; recompute the fingerprint with `material_diff.material_basis` / `pass1.material_fingerprint` and mark each row `verified` only when it matches the stored `material_fingerprint`. Fall back to the nearest `SNAPSHOT.compiled_state.description` and mark `unverified` when no exact match is found.\n3. Emit a manifest (`docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/corpus-<date>.manifest.json`: per-store counts, verdict/schema/cohort/model histograms, verification coverage, content hash) and a compact JSONL corpus (one row per review with findings, verification vectors, material text) under a git-ignored cache dir with the manifest hash as the reproducibility key. Assume rebuild-from-manifest is deterministic; the JSONL itself is not committed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__init__.py`, `corpus.py` (new)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/corpus-*.manifest.json` (new)\n- `.gitignore` (replay cache dir)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_corpus.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: a fixture store with one tree sidecar, one history-deleted sidecar, one compacted ticket → all three enumerated; fingerprint verification passes for a ticket whose EDIT history is intact and is marked `unverified` for one that was snapshotted with a later edit; v1 sidecars are loaded with the missing fields marked absent, not defaulted. Empty store → empty manifest, exit 0. Integration (manual, recorded in the manifest): a full build over both real stores.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Running the builder over the rebar and legacy-modernization-navigator stores produces a manifest whose sidecar count is ≥ the tree count plus the history-recovered count, with per-store and per-schema totals; checked by reading the manifest.\n- [ ] ≥95% of v2 sidecars have their reviewed material reconstructed and `verified` against `material_fingerprint`; checked by the manifest's `verified_ratio`.\n- [ ] Rebuilding from the same store refs yields an identical manifest content hash; checked by running twice and diffing.\n- [ ] The builder makes no LLM calls and needs no network beyond a local git fetch; checked by running with no provider credentials.\n- [ ] Unit tests above pass in `make test`.","id":"471c-f71f-342c-45ed","parent_id":"759e-7dc1-675c-4877","priority":1,"tags":["plan-review","evals","corpus"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Freeze the replayable plan-review corpus: both stores, git-recovered sidecars, fingerprint-verified plan text (zero LLM)"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788029097248845542,"uuid":"b122eae8-01c4-4e34-bc9c-feafb4d00c15"}